WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A pendulum swings. The hand appears still.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
In 1852, Carpenter studied how suggestion might influence movement without a felt decision.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
In 1854, Chevreul asked what the experiment—not the story—could establish.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Later laboratory work measured the pendulum illusion, including changes with attention.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000
A visible swing can be real while its interpretation is mistaken.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Let the question outlast the spectacle. Final Vestige: investigate the cause.
